IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part I, Division E, "Refunds of Overpayments": sections 38 and 39. LAYER 1, from the text alone.
--
-- Section 38 says when the Minister must or may refund contributions paid or deducted in excess: to an employee (who has made
-- an overpayment, or whose deductions exceed what section 8 requires), to an employer (remitted more than section 9 requires,
-- or a section 21.01 amount), and to a self-employed person. It sets the time for applying (four years after the end of the year,
-- or ten years for an employee notified after 1 September 2010 of a disability pension decision), lets the Minister recover an
-- excess refund, apply a refund to another debt to the Crown, and pay interest on a refund. Section 39 deals with refunds under
-- an agreement with a province that has its own pension plan.
--
-- The amounts the Act requires of an employee (section 8), an employer (section 9) and a self-employed person (section 10),
-- the "excess referred to in subsection 8(2)", the prescribed interest rate and period (Regulations sections 35 and 36, piece cr1),
-- and what the Minister is "satisfied" of, are plain inputs. A "may" is a BOOLEAN that the power exists, a "must" a BOOLEAN that the
-- duty arises, and an amount is a separate NUMBER rule, so the rules read from the person's side (what am I owed, by when).
-- Every rule is constitutive. A time limit "not later than N years after the end of the year" ends on 31 December of year + N.

§ `Division E -- Refunds of Overpayments`

§§ `s 38(1) to (3) -- the employee`

-- The time to apply: four years after the end of the year, or ten years "in the case of an employee who, in respect of a
-- disability pension, is notified after September 1, 2010 of a decision under subsection 60(7) or 81(2), a decision under
-- subsection 82(11) or 83(11) as those subsections read immediately before their repeal or a decision under section 54 or 59
-- of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act". The same words recur in subsections (3) and (4); one rule
-- states them and the three call it. A notification on 1 September 2010 itself is not "after" it (fork F24).
-- src:841 | Refund of overpayment
-- src:842 | 38 (1) If an overpayment has been made by an employee on account of the employee’s contributions under this Act for a year, the Minister must, if application in writing is made to the Minister by the employee not later than four years — or, in the case of an employee who, in respect of a disability pension, is notified after September 1, 2010 of a decision under subsection 60(7) or 81(2), a decision under subsection 82(11) or 83(11) as those subsections read immediately before their repeal or a decision under section 54 or 59 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act, 10 years — after the end of the year, refund to the employee the amount of the overpayment.
@ref Act s 38(1) (src:841-842)
GIVEN `the day the employee was notified, in respect of a disability pension, of a decision listed in section 38, if the employee was` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 38(1) — the number of years after the end of the year within which the application must be made` `the day the employee was notified, in respect of a disability pension, of a decision listed in section 38, if the employee was` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the employee was notified, in respect of a disability pension, of a decision listed in section 38, if the employee was`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 4
    WHEN JUST notified THEN
        IF notified GREATER THAN (YMD 2010 9 1)
        THEN 10
        ELSE 4

@ref Act s 38(1) (src:841-842)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the day the employee was notified, in respect of a disability pension, of a decision listed in section 38, if the employee was` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 38(1) — the last day for the employee to apply for a refund of the overpayment` year `the day the employee was notified, in respect of a disability pension, of a decision listed in section 38, if the employee was` MEANS
    `s 2(1) — the last day of a year` (year PLUS (`s 38(1) — the number of years after the end of the year within which the application must be made` `the day the employee was notified, in respect of a disability pension, of a decision listed in section 38, if the employee was`))

@ref Act s 38(1) (src:841-842)
GIVEN `an overpayment has been made by the employee on account of the employee's contributions for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee applied in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      year IS A NUMBER
      `the day the employee applied` IS A DATE
      `the day the employee was notified, in respect of a disability pension, of a decision listed in section 38, if the employee was` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38(1) — the Minister must refund the overpayment to the employee` `an overpayment has been made by the employee on account of the employee's contributions for the year` `the employee applied in writing to the Minister` year `the day the employee applied` `the day the employee was notified, in respect of a disability pension, of a decision listed in section 38, if the employee was` MEANS
        `an overpayment has been made by the employee on account of the employee's contributions for the year`
    AND `the employee applied in writing to the Minister`
    AND `the day the employee applied` AT MOST (`s 38(1) — the last day for the employee to apply for a refund of the overpayment` year `the day the employee was notified, in respect of a disability pension, of a decision listed in section 38, if the employee was`)

@ref Act s 38(1) (src:841-842)
GIVEN `the Minister must refund the overpayment under subsection 38(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the overpayment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 38(1) — the amount the Minister must refund to the employee` `the Minister must refund the overpayment under subsection 38(1)` `the amount of the overpayment` MEANS
    IF `the Minister must refund the overpayment under subsection 38(1)`
    THEN `the amount of the overpayment`
    ELSE 0

-- src:843 | Refund after decision on appeal
-- src:844 | (2) If an amount on account of contributions is deducted from the remuneration of an employee or is paid by an employer with respect to an employee, and it is decided by a decision on an appeal made under section 27, 27.1 or 28 that the amount exceeds the amount required by this Act to be deducted or paid, the Minister shall refund the excess if the employee or employer applies for it in writing to the Minister not later than 30 days after the decision is communicated to the employee or employer, as the case may be.
@ref Act s 38(2) (src:843-844)
GIVEN `an amount on account of contributions was deducted from the remuneration of an employee or paid by an employer with respect to the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was decided on an appeal under section 27, 27.1 or 28 that the amount exceeds the amount required by this Act to be deducted or paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee or employer applied in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the decision was communicated to the employee or employer` IS A DATE
      `the day the employee or employer applied` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38(2) — the Minister must refund the excess after the decision on appeal` `an amount on account of contributions was deducted from the remuneration of an employee or paid by an employer with respect to the employee` `it was decided on an appeal under section 27, 27.1 or 28 that the amount exceeds the amount required by this Act to be deducted or paid` `the employee or employer applied in writing to the Minister` `the day the decision was communicated to the employee or employer` `the day the employee or employer applied` MEANS
        `an amount on account of contributions was deducted from the remuneration of an employee or paid by an employer with respect to the employee`
    AND `it was decided on an appeal under section 27, 27.1 or 28 that the amount exceeds the amount required by this Act to be deducted or paid`
    AND `the employee or employer applied in writing to the Minister`
    AND `a date is within a time limit after a start date`
            `the day the employee or employer applied`
            `the day the decision was communicated to the employee or employer`
            (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 30)

@ref Act s 38(2) (src:843-844)
GIVEN `the Minister must refund the excess under subsection 38(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount deducted or paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount required by this Act to be deducted or paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 38(2) — the amount of the excess the Minister must refund` `the Minister must refund the excess under subsection 38(2)` `the amount deducted or paid` `the amount required by this Act to be deducted or paid` MEANS
    IF `the Minister must refund the excess under subsection 38(2)`
    THEN max 0 (`the amount deducted or paid` MINUS `the amount required by this Act to be deducted or paid`)
    ELSE 0

-- (3): "if an employee applies to the Minister and satisfies the Minister that, for any year, the amount deducted from the
-- employee's remuneration exceeds the contributions for the year required of the employee under section 8, the Minister may
-- refund the amount of the excess". Whether the Minister is satisfied is the Minister's judgment: a conditional input.
-- src:845 | Refund of excess — employee
-- src:846 | (3) Despite anything in this Part, if an employee applies to the Minister and satisfies the Minister that, for any year, the amount deducted from the employee’s remuneration exceeds the contributions for the year required of the employee under section 8, the Minister may refund the amount of the excess. The application must be made within four years — or, in the case of an employee who, in respect of a disability pension, is notified after September 1, 2010 of a decision under subsection 60(7) or 81(2), a decision under subsection 82(11) or 83(11) as those subsections read immediately before their repeal or a decision under section 54 or 59 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act, 10 years — after the end of the year.
@ref Act s 38(3) (src:845-846)
GIVEN `the employee applied to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the amount deducted from the employee's remuneration for the year exceeds the contributions for the year required of the employee under section 8` IS A BOOLEAN
      year IS A NUMBER
      `the day the employee applied` IS A DATE
      `the day the employee was notified, in respect of a disability pension, of a decision listed in section 38, if the employee was` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38(3) — the Minister may refund the excess to the employee` `the employee applied to the Minister` `the Minister is satisfied that the amount deducted from the employee's remuneration for the year exceeds the contributions for the year required of the employee under section 8` year `the day the employee applied` `the day the employee was notified, in respect of a disability pension, of a decision listed in section 38, if the employee was` MEANS
        `the employee applied to the Minister`
    AND `the Minister is satisfied that the amount deducted from the employee's remuneration for the year exceeds the contributions for the year required of the employee under section 8`
    AND `the day the employee applied` AT MOST (`s 38(1) — the last day for the employee to apply for a refund of the overpayment` year `the day the employee was notified, in respect of a disability pension, of a decision listed in section 38, if the employee was`)

@ref Act s 38(3) (src:845-846)
GIVEN `the amount deducted from the employee's remuneration for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributions for the year required of the employee under section 8` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: section 8 (piece cp1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 38(3) — the amount of the excess the Minister may refund to the employee` `the amount deducted from the employee's remuneration for the year` `the contributions for the year required of the employee under section 8` MEANS
    max 0 (`the amount deducted from the employee's remuneration for the year` MINUS `the contributions for the year required of the employee under section 8`)

§§ `s 38(3.1) to (3.3) -- the employer`

-- src:847 | Refund of amount remitted in excess — employer
-- src:848 | (3.1) Subject to subsection (3.2) but despite any other provision of this Part, if an employer applies to the Minister and satisfies the Minister that, for any year, the amount remitted by the employer as the employer’s contributions with respect to an employee exceeds the contributions for the year required of the employer under section 9 with respect to the employee, the Minister may refund the amount of the excess. The application must be made within four years after the end of the year.
@ref Act s 38(3.1) (src:847-848)
GIVEN `the employer applied to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the amount remitted by the employer as the employer's contributions with respect to the employee for the year exceeds the contributions for the year required of the employer under section 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      year IS A NUMBER
      `the day the employer applied` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38(3.1) — the Minister may refund the excess to the employer` `the employer applied to the Minister` `the Minister is satisfied that the amount remitted by the employer as the employer's contributions with respect to the employee for the year exceeds the contributions for the year required of the employer under section 9` year `the day the employer applied` MEANS
        `the employer applied to the Minister`
    AND `the Minister is satisfied that the amount remitted by the employer as the employer's contributions with respect to the employee for the year exceeds the contributions for the year required of the employer under section 9`
    AND `the day the employer applied` AT MOST (`s 2(1) — the last day of a year` (year PLUS 4))

@ref Act s 38(3.1) (src:847-848)
GIVEN `the amount remitted by the employer as the employer's contributions with respect to the employee for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributions for the year required of the employer under section 9 with respect to the employee` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: section 9 (piece cp1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 38(3.1) — the amount of the excess the Minister may refund to the employer` `the amount remitted by the employer as the employer's contributions with respect to the employee for the year` `the contributions for the year required of the employer under section 9 with respect to the employee` MEANS
    max 0 (`the amount remitted by the employer as the employer's contributions with respect to the employee for the year` MINUS `the contributions for the year required of the employer under section 9 with respect to the employee`)

-- src:849 | No refund of employers’ contributions
-- src:850 | (3.2) No refund may be made of any contribution required to be made as an employer’s contribution under section 9.
@ref Act s 38(3.2) (src:849-850)
GIVEN `the amount is a contribution required to be made as an employer's contribution under section 9` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38(3.2) — no refund may be made of the amount` `the amount is a contribution required to be made as an employer's contribution under section 9` MEANS
    `the amount is a contribution required to be made as an employer's contribution under section 9`

-- src:851 | Refund — section 21.01 amounts
-- src:852 | (3.3) If an amount remitted by an employer is deemed under section 21.01 not to have been deducted, the Minister may refund that amount to the employer if the employer applies to the Minister for the refund within four years after the end of the year for which the amount was remitted.
@ref Act s 38(3.3) (src:851-852)
GIVEN `an amount remitted by the employer is deemed under section 21.01 not to have been deducted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer applied to the Minister for the refund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the year for which the amount was remitted` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the employer applied` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38(3.3) — the Minister may refund the section 21.01 amount to the employer` `an amount remitted by the employer is deemed under section 21.01 not to have been deducted` `the employer applied to the Minister for the refund` `the year for which the amount was remitted` `the day the employer applied` MEANS
        `an amount remitted by the employer is deemed under section 21.01 not to have been deducted`
    AND `the employer applied to the Minister for the refund`
    AND `the day the employer applied` AT MOST (`s 2(1) — the last day of a year` (`the year for which the amount was remitted` PLUS 4))

§§ `s 38(4) and (4.1) -- the self-employed person`

