      `the Minister has sent the notice of assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor applied in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      year IS A NUMBER
      `the day the contributor applied` IS A DATE
      `the day the contributor was notified, in respect of a disability pension, of a decision listed in section 38, if the contributor was` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38(4)(b) — the Minister must refund the excess after sending the notice of assessment` `the person has paid, on account of the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings, an amount in excess of the contributions` `the Minister has sent the notice of assessment` `the contributor applied in writing to the Minister` year `the day the contributor applied` `the day the contributor was notified, in respect of a disability pension, of a decision listed in section 38, if the contributor was` MEANS
        `the person has paid, on account of the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings, an amount in excess of the contributions`
    AND `the Minister has sent the notice of assessment`
    AND `the contributor applied in writing to the Minister`
    AND `the day the contributor applied` AT MOST (`s 38(1) — the last day for the employee to apply for a refund of the overpayment` year `the day the contributor was notified, in respect of a disability pension, of a decision listed in section 38, if the contributor was`)

@ref Act s 38(4) (src:853-856)
GIVEN `the amount the person has paid on account of the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributions required to be made by the person for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: section 10 (piece cp1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 38(4) — the part of the amount paid that is in excess of the contributions` `the amount the person has paid on account of the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` `the contributions required to be made by the person for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` MEANS
    max 0 (`the amount the person has paid on account of the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` MINUS `the contributions required to be made by the person for the year in respect of self-employed earnings`)

-- src:857 | Refund after correction of record of earnings
-- src:858 | (4.1) Where an amount on account of a contribution is paid by a person in respect of self-employed earnings or is deducted from the remuneration of an employee and the Minister determines, taking into consideration an amendment made under section 97 to the Record of Earnings, that the amount paid or deducted is in excess of the amount required by this Act to be paid or deducted, the Minister may refund the excess.
@ref Act s 38(4.1) (src:857-858)
GIVEN `an amount on account of a contribution was paid by a person in respect of self-employed earnings or deducted from the remuneration of an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister determines, taking into consideration an amendment made under section 97 to the Record of Earnings, that the amount paid or deducted is in excess of the amount required by this Act to be paid or deducted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38(4.1) — the Minister may refund the excess after the Record of Earnings is corrected` `an amount on account of a contribution was paid by a person in respect of self-employed earnings or deducted from the remuneration of an employee` `the Minister determines, taking into consideration an amendment made under section 97 to the Record of Earnings, that the amount paid or deducted is in excess of the amount required by this Act to be paid or deducted` MEANS
        `an amount on account of a contribution was paid by a person in respect of self-employed earnings or deducted from the remuneration of an employee`
    AND `the Minister determines, taking into consideration an amendment made under section 97 to the Record of Earnings, that the amount paid or deducted is in excess of the amount required by this Act to be paid or deducted`

§§ `s 38(5) to (8) -- recovery, set-off and interest`

-- src:859 | Recovery of amount refunded or credited on liability
-- src:860 | (5) If an application under this section has been made to the Minister for a refund of any amount deducted on account of an employee’s contributions for a year and, whether on the basis of incorrect or incomplete information contained in the application or otherwise, the Minister has refunded an amount to the employee, or applied an amount to a liability of the employee to Her Majesty in right of Canada, in excess of the amount that should have been refunded or applied, the amount of the excess may be recovered at any time from the employee as a debt due to Her Majesty.
@ref Act s 38(5) (src:859-860)
GIVEN `an application under section 38 was made for a refund of an amount deducted on account of an employee's contributions for a year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount the Minister refunded to the employee or applied to a liability of the employee to Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount that should have been refunded or applied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 38(5) — the excess that may be recovered at any time from the employee as a debt due to Her Majesty` `an application under section 38 was made for a refund of an amount deducted on account of an employee's contributions for a year` `the amount the Minister refunded to the employee or applied to a liability of the employee to Her Majesty in right of Canada` `the amount that should have been refunded or applied` MEANS
    IF `an application under section 38 was made for a refund of an amount deducted on account of an employee's contributions for a year`
    THEN max 0 (`the amount the Minister refunded to the employee or applied to a liability of the employee to Her Majesty in right of Canada` MINUS `the amount that should have been refunded or applied`)
    ELSE 0

-- src:861 | Application of refund to other debts
-- src:862 | (6) Instead of making a refund that might otherwise be made under this section, the Minister may, where the person to whom the refund is payable is liable or about to become liable to make any payment to Her Majesty in right of Canada, apply the amount of the refund to that liability and notify the person of that action.
@ref Act s 38(6) (src:861-862)
GIVEN `a refund might otherwise be made under section 38` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person to whom the refund is payable is liable or about to become liable to make a payment to Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38(6) — the Minister may apply the refund to the person's liability instead of making the refund` `a refund might otherwise be made under section 38` `the person to whom the refund is payable is liable or about to become liable to make a payment to Her Majesty in right of Canada` MEANS
        `a refund might otherwise be made under section 38`
    AND `the person to whom the refund is payable is liable or about to become liable to make a payment to Her Majesty in right of Canada`

-- The text applies "the amount of the refund" to the liability and says nothing of a refund larger than the liability: the amount
-- applied is the lesser, and the rest is still refundable (fork F25).
@ref Act s 38(6) (src:861-862)
GIVEN `the Minister may apply the refund under subsection 38(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the refund` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the liability to Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 38(6) — the amount of the refund applied to the liability` `the Minister may apply the refund under subsection 38(6)` `the amount of the refund` `the amount of the liability to Her Majesty in right of Canada` MEANS
    IF `the Minister may apply the refund under subsection 38(6)`
    THEN min `the amount of the refund` `the amount of the liability to Her Majesty in right of Canada`
    ELSE 0

@ref Act s 38(6) (src:861-862)
GIVEN `the Minister applied the refund to the person's liability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38(6) — the Minister must notify the person of the application of the refund` `the Minister applied the refund to the person's liability` MEANS
    `the Minister applied the refund to the person's liability`

-- (7): interest on an overpayment refunded or applied, "at a prescribed rate per annum under the circumstances and for the period
-- or periods determined as prescribed", except that (a) none is paid if it is less than one dollar, and (b) none on an amount
-- refundable under (4.1). The rate and the day the period begins are prescribed by Regulations sections 35 and 36 (piece cr1).
-- src:863 | Interest on overpayments
-- src:864 | (7) If an amount in respect of an overpayment is refunded or applied under this Act to any other liability, interest shall be paid or applied on the amount at a prescribed rate per annum under the circumstances and for the period or periods determined as prescribed, except that
-- src:865 | (a) no interest shall be paid or applied if the amount of the interest is less than one dollar; and
-- src:866 | (b) no interest shall be paid or applied on an amount that is refundable under subsection (4.1).
@ref Act s 38(7) (src:863-866)
GIVEN `an amount in respect of an overpayment is refunded or applied under this Act to any other liability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the overpayment refunded or applied` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the period of interest begins` IS A DATE -- out of range: Regulations section 35 (piece cr1)
      `the day the amount is refunded or applied` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed rate of interest per annum` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: Regulations section 36 (piece cr1)
      `the amount is refundable under subsection 38(4.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount is an amount referred to in subsection 38(3.3) that is refunded or applied under this Act to any other liability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 38(7) — the interest paid or applied on the overpayment` `an amount in respect of an overpayment is refunded or applied under this Act to any other liability` `the amount of the overpayment refunded or applied` `the day the period of interest begins` `the day the amount is refunded or applied` `the prescribed rate of interest per annum` `the amount is refundable under subsection 38(4.1)` `the amount is an amount referred to in subsection 38(3.3) that is refunded or applied under this Act to any other liability` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `an amount in respect of an overpayment is refunded or applied under this Act to any other liability`) THEN 0
        IF `the amount is refundable under subsection 38(4.1)` THEN 0
        IF `s 38(8) — subsection 38(7) does not apply to the amount` `the amount is an amount referred to in subsection 38(3.3) that is refunded or applied under this Act to any other liability` THEN 0
        IF `the interest before the dollar floor` LESS THAN 1 THEN 0
        OTHERWISE `the interest before the dollar floor`
    WHERE
        `the interest before the dollar floor` MEANS
            `the amount of the overpayment refunded or applied`
                TIMES `the prescribed rate of interest per annum`
                TIMES ((max 0 (Day `the day the amount is refunded or applied` MINUS Day `the day the period of interest begins`)) DIVIDED BY 365)

-- src:867 | Non-application — subsection (7)
-- src:868 | (8) Subsection (7) does not apply in respect of an amount referred to in subsection (3.3) that is refunded or applied under this Act to any other liability.
@ref Act s 38(8) (src:867-868)
GIVEN `the amount is an amount referred to in subsection 38(3.3) that is refunded or applied under this Act to any other liability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38(8) — subsection 38(7) does not apply to the amount` `the amount is an amount referred to in subsection 38(3.3) that is refunded or applied under this Act to any other liability` MEANS
    `the amount is an amount referred to in subsection 38(3.3) that is refunded or applied under this Act to any other liability`

§§ `s 39 -- refunds under an agreement with a province`

-- src:869 | Refund of overpayment in accordance with agreement
-- src:870 | 39 (1) Despite anything in this Act, if an overpayment has been made by an employee on account of the employee’s contributions for a year under this Act, the Minister may, in accordance with any agreement that may be entered into by the Minister with the approval of the Governor in Council with the appropriate authority of a province having the administration of the provincial pension plan referred to in subsection 8(2), if application in writing is made to the Minister by the employee not later than four years after the end of the year, refund to the employee the whole amount of the excess referred to in that subsection, in which case the whole of that amount is deemed to be an overpayment made by the employee on account of the employee’s contributions for that year under this Act.
@ref Act s 39(1) (src:869-870)
GIVEN `an overpayment has been made by the employee on account of the employee's contributions for the year under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has entered into an agreement with the approval of the Governor in Council with the appropriate authority of a province having the administration of the provincial pension plan referred to in subsection 8(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee applied in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      year IS A NUMBER
      `the day the employee applied` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(1) — the Minister may refund the whole amount of the excess to the employee in accordance with the agreement` `an overpayment has been made by the employee on account of the employee's contributions for the year under this Act` `the Minister has entered into an agreement with the approval of the Governor in Council with the appropriate authority of a province having the administration of the provincial pension plan referred to in subsection 8(2)` `the employee applied in writing to the Minister` year `the day the employee applied` MEANS
        `an overpayment has been made by the employee on account of the employee's contributions for the year under this Act`
    AND `the Minister has entered into an agreement with the approval of the Governor in Council with the appropriate authority of a province having the administration of the provincial pension plan referred to in subsection 8(2)`
    AND `the employee applied in writing to the Minister`
    AND `the day the employee applied` AT MOST (`s 2(1) — the last day of a year` (year PLUS 4))

-- "in which case the whole of that amount is deemed to be an overpayment made by the employee ... under this Act".
@ref Act s 39(1) (src:869-870)
GIVEN `the Minister refunds the whole amount of the excess referred to in subsection 8(2) under the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the excess referred to in subsection 8(2)` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: subsection 8(2) (piece cp1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 39(1) — the amount deemed to be an overpayment made by the employee under this Act` `the Minister refunds the whole amount of the excess referred to in subsection 8(2) under the agreement` `the excess referred to in subsection 8(2)` MEANS
    IF `the Minister refunds the whole amount of the excess referred to in subsection 8(2) under the agreement`
    THEN `the excess referred to in subsection 8(2)`
    ELSE 0

-- src:871 | Saving
-- src:872 | (2) If, in accordance with any agreement entered into under subsection (1), the appropriate authority of a province has refunded to an employee the whole amount of the excess referred to in subsection 8(2) with respect to that employee, the whole of that amount is deemed to be an overpayment made by the employee on account of the employee’s contributions for that year under the provincial pension plan referred to in that subsection.
@ref Act s 39(2) (src:871-872)
GIVEN `the appropriate authority of a province has refunded to the employee the whole amount of the excess referred to in subsection 8(2) in accordance with an agreement entered into under subsection 39(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the excess referred to in subsection 8(2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 39(2) — the amount deemed to be an overpayment made by the employee under the provincial pension plan` `the appropriate authority of a province has refunded to the employee the whole amount of the excess referred to in subsection 8(2) in accordance with an agreement entered into under subsection 39(1)` `the excess referred to in subsection 8(2)` MEANS
    IF `the appropriate authority of a province has refunded to the employee the whole amount of the excess referred to in subsection 8(2) in accordance with an agreement entered into under subsection 39(1)`
    THEN `the excess referred to in subsection 8(2)`
    ELSE 0

-- src:873 | Provision for making of financial adjustments
-- src:874 | (3) Any agreement entered into under subsection (1) may provide for the making of any financial adjustments required to be made by reason of any payments made to employees in accordance with that agreement and for the crediting or charging of the amount of those adjustments to the Canada Pension Plan Account or the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account, as the case may be.
@ref Act s 39(3) (src:873-874)
GIVEN `the agreement was entered into under subsection 39(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial adjustments are required by reason of payments made to employees in accordance with the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(3) — the agreement may provide for the financial adjustments and for crediting or charging them to the Canada Pension Plan Account or the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` `the agreement was entered into under subsection 39(1)` `the financial adjustments are required by reason of payments made to employees in accordance with the agreement` MEANS
        `the agreement was entered into under subsection 39(1)`
    AND `the financial adjustments are required by reason of payments made to employees in accordance with the agreement`
